{start_of_verse}
I ain't [D]rich, but I damn sure wanna [G]be
[D]Working like a dog all day, ain't working for [A]me
I wish I had a [D]rich uncle that'd kick the bucket
And that I was sitting on a [G]pile like Warren Buffett
[D]I know everybody says money can't buy [A]happiness
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
But it could buy me a [D]boat, it could buy me a [G]truck to pull it
It could buy me a [D]Yeti 110 iced down with some Silver [A]Bullets
Yeah, I [D]know what they say, money can't buy every[G]thing
Well, maybe [D]so, but it could buy me a [A]boat
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
They call me [D]redneck, white trash and blue [G]collar
But I could [D]change all that if I had a couple million [A]dollars
I keep [D]hearing that money is the root of all evil
And you can't fit a [G]camel through the eye of a needle
I'm sure that's probably [D]true, but it still sounds pretty [A]cool
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
'Cause it could buy me a [D]boat, it could buy me a [G]truck to pull it
It could buy me a [D]Yeti 110 iced down with some Silver [A]Bullets
Yeah, I [D]know what they say, money can't buy every[G]thing
Well, maybe [D]so, but it could buy me a [A]boat
{end_of_chorus}

